---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { dataMode } from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="Methodology"><div class="shell page-intro"><div class="section-label">HOW WE TRACK / METHODOLOGY</div><h1>Evidence before<br /><em>assumption.</em></h1><p>TrackYourInfra is designed as a public record. A useful update needs a source, a date and enough context for someone else to check it.</p></div><div class="shell methodology-layout"><nav class="method-nav" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#demonstration-data">Demonstration data</a><a href="#status">Project status</a><a href="#confidence">Confidence</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a><a href="#contribute">Contribution roadmap</a></nav><div class="method-content"><section id="demonstration-data"><div class="section-label">01 / CURRENT DATA</div><h2>Separate demonstration and real records.</h2><p>{dataMode === "demo" ? "The three demo corridors, routes, dates, costs and progress values are invented to test the interface. They are not real project claims." : "The public dataset includes source-backed records. Demo corridors are stored separately and are not shown in this mode. Unverified alignments and values stay blank."}</p><p>The first real pilot record is Bengaluru Metro Phase 3. Its route geometry is intentionally absent until a source-backed alignment is reviewed.</p></section><section id="status"><div class="section-label">02 / LIFECYCLE</div><h2>Status describes a stage.</h2><div class="definition-grid"><div><strong>Proposed</strong><p>Publicly discussed; formal approval not established.</p></div><div><strong>Approved</strong><p>Relevant authority has formally approved it.</p></div><div><strong>Funded</strong><p>Funding has been confirmed.</p></div><div><strong>Tendering</strong><p>Procurement is underway.</p></div><div><strong>Under construction</strong><p>Physical work has started.</p></div><div><strong>Partially operational</strong><p>Some sections are open.</p></div><div><strong>Operational</strong><p>The tracked scope is open.</p></div><div><strong>Delayed / cancelled</strong><p>A dated source confirms the change.</p></div></div></section><section id="confidence"><div class="section-label">03 / CONFIDENCE</div><h2>Confidence is about evidence.</h2><p><strong>High</strong> means supported by primary documents or multiple corroborating sources. <strong>Medium</strong> means credible reporting or verified observations. <strong>Low</strong> means an early or illustrative report requiring further review. A confidence label applies to a particular claim, not to every fact on a page.</p></section><section id="sources"><div class="section-label">04 / PROVENANCE</div><h2>Keep the trail visible.</h2><p>For each important claim, the site records its source, publication date, status date and last update. Unknown values stay blank rather than being inferred. Later revisions should remain visible through the public repository history.</p></section><section id="contribute"><div class="section-label">05 / WHAT'S NEXT</div><h2>Community review comes next.</h2><p>Phase 2 uses GitHub Issue Forms, pull request review and source-backed project files. The owner/name must be configured before report links can work. The website and data live in one open MIT licensed repository.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/projects">Explore the prototype <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section></div></div></Base>
